-- title:
--   Algebraic integrality of a prime-to-p multiple of ⟨ e⟩ f∣ W_d
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a positive integer $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing the kernel of reduction, in the sense that every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ whose image under `ZMod.unitsMap` along $M/p \mid M$ is $1$ lies in $H$. Let $W_d$ be an Atkin–Lehner datum for the pair $(M, M/p)$, that is, a natural number $R$ with $M = (M/p) \cdot R$ together with integers $a, b$ satisfying $(M/p)a - Rb = 1$, let $e \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and let $f$ be a weight-$2$ cusp form for the subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, the image in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under the character $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ given by the lower-right entry. Assume $f$ lies in [`CuspForm.twoCuspIntegralSet M H 2 p (⊥ : Subring ℂ)`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L54): for every element $t$ of the Hecke ring `heckeRingH M H 2` (the subring of $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphisms generated by the Hecke generators), every Atkin–Lehner datum $W$ for $(M, p)$ and every $n$, the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $t f$ and of $(t f) \mid_2 W$ both lie in the bottom subring of $\mathbb{C}$, i.e. are rational integers. Then there exists $D \in \mathbb{N}$ with $p \nmid D$ and a formal power series over the integral closure $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ whose image under the coefficientwise map to $\mathbb{C}$ is the $q$-expansion of period $1$ of $D \cdot \bigl( (\langle e \rangle f) \mid_2 W_d \bigr)$, where $\langle e \rangle =$ [`CuspForm.diamondLinH 2 e`](def/CuspForm_HeckeOperatorFormsGammaH.html#L132) is the weight-$2$ slash by a lift of $e$ to $\Gamma_0(M)$ (and the zero map if the cusp-stability predicate `StableD` fails), and $\mid_2 W_d$ is the weight-$2$ slash by the real matrix attached to $W_d$.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion integrality statement used when an Atkin–Lehner translate of a diamond translate of a two-cusp integral weight-$2$ form is compared with an integral model: some multiple of the translate, by an integer prime to $p$, has algebraic-integer Fourier coefficients at $\infty$. It feeds the constructions on modular curves that pin Atkin–Lehner data and compare Hecke correspondences in characteristic $\ell$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_not_dvd_and_algInt_qExpansion_smul_alSlash_diamond_of_mem_twoCuspIntegralSet_of_ker_le.lean

